{"kind":"assert","text":"O3 approval 353c62ec carries one finding that blocks O4, not O3's landing.\n\nAnyone can fill client registration for good. POST /oauth/register needs no credential and writes to one registry, oauth-public-clients-1. That registry holds at most 1,000 clients and never removes one. So 1,000 anonymous requests end dynamic registration on the Worker. Each later request answers 503 with Retry-After, but no retry succeeds, and no route or setting clears the table. Claude and ChatGPT use metadata documents and keep working. Goose and other clients that register do not.\n\nBefore O4 opens a Worker, a reviewed head should make a full registry recoverable, with a control in which client 1,001 succeeds after an unused registration expires.","body":{"to":"planner"}}